posits, we want to select where the 60 ETH         should come from. The funds will all be held in the LP but we are storing how many validators are spun up per source on the contract.         We simply check which of the sources is below their target allocation and allocate the deposits to it.","returns":{"_0":"The chosen source of funds (EETH or ETHER_FAN)"}},"batchApproveRegistration(uint256[],bytes[],bytes[])":{"details":"This gets called by the Oracle and only when it has confirmed the withdraw credentials of the 1 ETH deposit in the registration         phase match the withdraw credentials stored on the beacon chain. This prevents a front-running attack.","params":{"_pubKey":"The pubKey for each validator being spun up.","_signature":"The signatures for each validator for the 31 ETH transaction that were emitted in the register phase","_validatorIds":"The IDs of the validators to be approved"}},"batchCancelDeposit(uint256[])":{"details":"This is called only in the BNFT player flow","params":{"_validatorIds":"The IDs to be cancelled"}},"batchDepositAsBnftHolder(uint256[],uint256)":{"details":"This function has multiple dependencies that need to be followed before this function will succeed. ","params":{"_candidateBidIds":"validator IDs that have been matched with the BNFT holder on the FE","_numberOfValidators":"how many validators the user wants to spin up. This can be less than the candidateBidIds length.          we may have more Ids sent in than needed to spin up incase some ids fail."},"returns":{"_0":"Array of bids that were successfully processed."}},"batchRegisterAsBnftHolder(bytes32,uint256[],(bytes,bytes,bytes32,string)[],bytes32[],bytes[])":{"details":"This function can only be called by a BNFT player on IDs that have been deposited.  ","params":{"_depositDataRootApproval":"The deposit data roots for each validator for the 31 ETH transaction which will happen in the approval         step. See the Staking Manager for details.","_depositRoot":"This is 